# Profile: optimal_limit -- the MAKER-FIRST arm of the execution A/B.
#
# Identical to `optimal` (2% x inv_z tilt, $25 cap, floored, no guards) except
# that orders POST instead of TAKE: a LIMIT at the signal's quote minus one
# tick, resting up to 20s, cancelled if it has not filled. A miss ends the
# round -- no retry, no crossing -- because crossing would pay the very spread
# the limit exists to avoid.
#
# Why: the measured cost of taking is 1.32/$1 of EV (EV +0.0431 at the quote
# vs +0.0300 at the price paid, median fill 175bps over the quote, worse on 78%
# of fills). A resting order pays OUR price, and the venue enforces priceLimit
# as a maximum while passing price improvement through -- verified live: a
# LIMIT capped at 0.50 filled at 0.0612.
#
# LIMIT is GTC (MARKET must be FOK), requires `priceLimit`, and has no ~1.5
# USDT minimum (MARKET does). Cancel is proven live over a hand-built request:
# the indexed brackets must reach the venue unencoded or it answers -1022.
#
# Control arm: `optimal_slip100` (market FOK, 100bps). Judge the arms on fill
# RATE and on `ev_at_fill` (the gate->fill field), never on P&L.
#
# Knobs only -- no keys, no endpoints, nothing secret. Apply with:
#   make config PROFILE=optimal_limit
order_type=limit
limit_offset=0.01
limit_wait_s=20.0
slippage_bps=100
sizing_mode=fraction